#!/bin/sh
# Nothing to do after a first installation (F58; SPEC design section 2). The account was created by pre_install. The hooks of systemd and
# dbus, which pacman runs after this script, do the rest on the paths this package ships: 30-systemd-daemon-reload-system (daemon-reload),
# dbus-reload (bus reload), 25-systemd-catalog (journal catalog). Repeating a call here would run it twice, and before the hook. The unit is
# never enabled or started: D-Bus activation and its socket start it. Nothing here touches the state directory. See docs/decisions/packaging.md.
# Only the socket of the Firefox snap (F173) is enabled and started, here: a new unit file is read from disk, so it needs no reload first.
systemctl enable custodio-firefox.socket || true
systemctl start custodio-firefox.socket || true
:
